# FIELD-MEM p4: every scene open is its own device-memory window. Proof: editor.log - one
# "[Memory] scene open #N '<scene>' ... (window opened)" per open; the last "scene open #3 'FIELD_Barn.desce' peak" <=
# the "scene open #1 'FIELD_Barn.desce' peak ... (window closed ...)" + 100 MB, owed at that peak < 50 MB.
# A driven session (--control-socket) shows no "Recover unsaved work?" modal ([Recovery] driven session line instead).
Дано run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn.desce"
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,900,2500
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.15,-1
Тогда 1_barn the scene opened: the field is drawn (grass to the far edge), no modal window, the editor alive
Когда run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Тогда 2_starter the second scene opened and draws, no modal window
Когда run Scene "Open Scene FIELD_Barn.desce"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,900,2500
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.15,-0.15,-1
Тогда 3_barn_again FIELD_Barn again: the field as in 1_barn, no modal window; open #3 peak <= open #1 peak + 100 MB in the log
